---
pre-compare: sort
---
from_file env("TENZIR_INPUT") {
  read_json
}
// The same stored-shape fixture with three post-stamp mutations applied
// in the store — the verification lane's threat model, one per break
// type. (1) The case-attest-1 open record's desc was edited after
// stamping with its attestation left stale: the per-record fingerprint
// recompute must flag it. (2) The case-attest-1 evidence record was
// deleted: the close record's prev_event no longer references its
// immediate predecessor, and the walk must flag the broken link. (3) The
// case-attest-4 open record was deleted: its close is now the first
// record the walk sees yet still references a predecessor, and the walk
// must flag the missing chain head. The determinism pair and the restart
// record ride along intact and must stay silent. Expected: the summary
// line plus three findings — fingerprint_mismatch on the case-attest-1
// open, chain_link_mismatch on the case-attest-1 close, and
// chain_head_missing on the case-attest-4 close.
fork {
  summarize records_checked = count()
  to_stdout { write_json }
}
homelab::investigations::ocsf::verify
// Findings only reach here (the walk drops intact records); pin the
// finding time for the baseline — the operator stamps now() live.
time = 2026-10-17T11:00:00Z
